course: dictionary
lesson: 11731
title: Aviation: flying and planes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aviation is a noun. It means flying aircraft, and everything to do with building, running and flying planes. When you meet this word, look at the words around it. «Aviation history is full of brave people who tried to fly.» The sentence tells you the topic is flying and planes.
explain: Look for clues in the words near it. «Pilots, engineers and mechanics all work in aviation.» Pilots fly planes, engineers design and build them, and mechanics fix them, so aviation covers all of this. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "flying planes and everything to do with them" still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Aviation often comes in phrases. «Civil aviation» is ordinary flying, such as passenger planes. «Aviation fuel» is the fuel that planes use. The word next to aviation tells you which part of flying the phrase is about.
fact: Aviation means flying aircraft and everything to do with building, running and flying planes.
fact: Aviation is a noun.
fact: The Wright brothers are famous in aviation history.
fact: Amelia Earhart is another famous name in aviation history.
fact: «Aviation fuel» is the fuel that planes use.
exercise: «Pilots, engineers and mechanics all work in aviation.» What does aviation mean here? | *Flying planes and everything to do with them | Cooking food on a long journey | Swimming in deep water | Reading old maps
exercise: The class studied aviation history this week. What were they learning about? | Ships sailing across the oceans | *Flying and planes through the past | Cars in a race | Trains on old railways
exercise: «The engineer checked the aviation fuel before the flight.» What is aviation fuel? | Sand for a sandcastle | Water for washing the windows | *Fuel that planes use | Fuel for cars and buses only
test: A pilot works in aviation. What does a pilot's job involve? | *Flying planes | Building bridges over rivers | Cooking dinner for passengers
test: Which lesson would you meet aviation in if you were learning how planes stay in the air? | Music | Art | Dance | *Science
exam: «The Wright brothers changed aviation forever.» What does aviation mean? | Painting pictures of the sea | *Flying planes and everything to do with them | Driving trains through tunnels | Cooking food for a crowd
